1016
00:46:27.160 --> 00:46:32.400
And when he leaves the conference room, he tells Dwight, it's over.

1017
00:46:32.900 --> 00:46:33.780
It's over.

1018
00:46:33.920 --> 00:46:38.680
And he means over between you and Angela, not me and Angela.

1019
00:46:38.840 --> 00:46:40.280
He's still going to marry Angela.

1020
00:46:40.680 --> 00:46:42.460
Well, Angela made a big case.

1021
00:46:42.620 --> 00:46:44.600
She was like, listen, we're at a crossroads here.

1022
00:46:44.600 --> 00:46:46.380
Let's prove all these people wrong.

1023
00:46:46.860 --> 00:46:51.100
Dwight makes a big declaration that Bernard will never be her last name.

1024
00:46:51.300 --> 00:46:52.880
They are going to stay together.

1025
00:46:53.100 --> 00:46:54.440
He is not going to give up.

1026
00:46:54.980 --> 00:46:56.640
Jenna, this was a much longer scene.

1027
00:46:57.060 --> 00:47:01.420
And when Dwight says a duel, we'll have a duel over Angela.

1028
00:47:01.600 --> 00:47:03.220
The winner gets Angela.

1029
00:47:03.920 --> 00:47:05.300
Stanley can't take it anymore.

1030
00:47:05.560 --> 00:47:07.020
He's going to call BS.

1031
00:47:07.460 --> 00:47:09.180
And he has this great moment.

1032
00:47:09.780 --> 00:47:11.040
Okay, we're not doing that.

1033
00:47:11.260 --> 00:47:12.140
Hang on, Pam.

1034
00:47:12.140 --> 00:47:15.560
Andy, do you fully understand that the prize is Angela?

1035
00:47:16.620 --> 00:47:18.380
So help me God, I do.

1036
00:47:18.980 --> 00:47:22.520
And Dwight, do you fully understand that the prize is Angela?

1037
00:47:22.760 --> 00:47:23.220
I do.

1038
00:47:24.440 --> 00:47:26.100
I say give them both guns.

1039
00:47:26.220 --> 00:47:26.700
Stanley.

1040
00:47:27.000 --> 00:47:27.680
Darwin, baby.

1041
00:47:28.120 --> 00:47:28.480
Darwin.

1042
00:47:31.880 --> 00:47:32.800
Darwin, baby.

1043
00:47:33.140 --> 00:47:33.480
Darwin.

1044
00:47:34.320 --> 00:47:35.860
I just love that moment.

1045
00:47:37.660 --> 00:47:41.840
Even Pam turns to Angela and is like, you have to stop this.

1046
00:47:42.160 --> 00:47:46.840
But Angela says, I will respect the results of the duel.

1047
00:47:47.300 --> 00:47:51.020
So, yeah, I remember us shooting this moment, Jenna.

1048
00:47:51.380 --> 00:47:54.320
But in my mind, there was more to the scene.

1049
00:47:54.320 --> 00:48:00.260
I went to the script, and there was an alt of this moment where Pam confronts Angela.

1050
00:48:00.540 --> 00:48:01.900
It didn't make it in.

1051
00:48:02.020 --> 00:48:03.760
And you have a whole speech.

1052
00:48:03.920 --> 00:48:05.620
And I called it, Preach, Pam!

1053
00:48:06.300 --> 00:48:08.680
This takes place in the break room.

1054
00:48:09.700 --> 00:48:10.680
Okay, Angela.

1055
00:48:10.820 --> 00:48:11.040
What?

1056
00:48:12.500 --> 00:48:14.380
You have to put a stop to this.

1057
00:48:15.160 --> 00:48:20.200
I admit, at first, I was blaming you for being selfish and dishoneSt.

1058
00:48:20.540 --> 00:48:22.780
But then I decided to put myself in your shoes.

1059
00:48:23.120 --> 00:48:24.620
I didn't ask you to do that.

1060
00:48:27.560 --> 00:48:28.380
I get it.

1061
00:48:29.020 --> 00:48:31.580
You're having a hard time choosing between Dwight and Andy.

1062
00:48:32.360 --> 00:48:34.920
For reasons that you must have about that.

1063
00:48:36.660 --> 00:48:38.240
But you have to make a decision, Angela.

1064
00:48:39.320 --> 00:48:41.180
Who would you rather go home to at night?

1065
00:48:42.080 --> 00:48:44.180
Who would you rather wake up with in the morning?

1066
00:48:44.960 --> 00:48:46.680
Marriage is a big deal, Angela.

1067
00:48:47.860 --> 00:48:49.980
Who do you see as the father of your children?

1068
00:48:50.660 --> 00:48:52.420
Who are you most proud of?

1069
00:48:53.900 --> 00:48:56.660
Who's most accepting of your...

1070
00:48:57.320 --> 00:48:57.800
quirkiness?

1071
00:49:00.760 --> 00:49:02.800
I don't see how any of that matters now.

1072
00:49:03.160 --> 00:49:03.580
Why not?

1073
00:49:04.100 --> 00:49:05.880
Two men are about to fight for my hand.

1074
00:49:06.340 --> 00:49:09.640
When it's over, I will respect one of them and pity the other.

1075
00:49:10.200 --> 00:49:11.000
Decision made.

1076
00:49:11.540 --> 00:49:11.900
Angela.

1077
00:49:17.200 --> 00:49:17.680
Wow.

1078
00:49:18.700 --> 00:49:19.180
Yeah.

1079
00:49:19.180 --> 00:49:26.180
I mean, Pam, like, really tried to show up for Angela in this moment.

1080
00:49:26.400 --> 00:49:27.820
Tried to empathize with her.

1081
00:49:27.980 --> 00:49:32.440
And what, you know, you guys are hearing it, but if you watch it, if you go to the deleted

1082
00:49:32.440 --> 00:49:37.220
scenes on the DVD, you see all of this emotion go across my face.

1083
00:49:37.680 --> 00:49:39.080
I'm clearly torn.

1084
00:49:39.380 --> 00:49:39.780
Yeah.

1085
00:49:39.780 --> 00:49:44.700
And it just really showed something you don't get to see that much in this.

1086
00:49:44.780 --> 00:49:48.560
You only see little moments that Angela is really struggling.

1087
00:49:48.560 --> 00:49:49.480
Yeah.

1088
00:49:49.900 --> 00:49:55.140
Well, Angela, when I was trading messages with Jen Salata about this episode, she was very

1089
00:49:55.140 --> 00:49:56.980
complimentary of your performance.

1090
00:49:57.420 --> 00:49:57.920
Oh.

1091
00:49:58.160 --> 00:50:04.900
She said that this episode was tricky and a lot rested on how your character would react

1092
00:50:04.900 --> 00:50:06.940
to these two men dueling over her.

1093
00:50:07.140 --> 00:50:08.940
She said she was really worried.

1094
00:50:08.940 --> 00:50:15.740
Like, how do you convince people that you would accept the results of a duel?

1095
00:50:16.480 --> 00:50:18.080
It's so crazy.

1096
00:50:18.640 --> 00:50:18.960
Yeah.

1097
00:50:19.260 --> 00:50:27.200
And she said, you know, there was this scene that really shows you stuffing down your real

1098
00:50:27.200 --> 00:50:27.760
feelings.

1099
00:50:28.020 --> 00:50:35.560
But she said that you were able to play it so perfectly in just your one line in the bullpen.

1100
00:50:35.560 --> 00:50:42.500
Jen, we so believed that your character would accept the results of a duel that it grounds

1101
00:50:42.500 --> 00:50:43.340
the whole episode.

1102
00:50:43.340 --> 00:50:46.060
And she was so grateful for your performance.

1103
00:50:46.840 --> 00:50:47.380
Oh, my gosh.

1104
00:50:47.380 --> 00:50:48.320
That's so nice.

1105
00:50:48.500 --> 00:50:48.600
Yeah.

1106
00:50:48.600 --> 00:50:49.200
Thank you, Jen.

1107
00:50:49.580 --> 00:50:54.920
Well, you know, what I thought about Angela is that she really loves Dwight.

1108
00:50:55.320 --> 00:51:01.300
She really thinks Andy is a better partner for her, like socially sort of acceptable and

1109
00:51:01.300 --> 00:51:01.960
all of that.

1110
00:51:01.960 --> 00:51:06.020
And she's really struggling about what's the right thing to do in her life.

1111
00:51:06.360 --> 00:51:11.640
And the duel for her is actually a relief because now she doesn't have to decide.

1112
00:51:12.120 --> 00:51:16.160
To her, this is like an institution that will decide for her.

1113
00:51:16.240 --> 00:51:17.460
And she's off the hook.

1114
00:51:17.580 --> 00:51:20.240
And I think that's why she was so willing to accept it.

1115
00:51:20.520 --> 00:51:26.940
We had some people write in wondering, were you secretly rooting for one man over the

1116
00:51:26.940 --> 00:51:27.160
other?

1117
00:51:27.380 --> 00:51:30.680
Do you think Angela Martin was secretly rooting for one person?

1118
00:51:31.240 --> 00:51:33.140
I think she was hoping Dwight would win.

1119
00:51:33.700 --> 00:51:39.620
For her, I just have this feeling that on paper, Andy Bernard is more presentable to

1120
00:51:39.620 --> 00:51:41.160
her family, right?

1121
00:51:41.320 --> 00:51:45.640
And makes more sense to Angela Martin's family and that they would be more accepting and

1122
00:51:45.640 --> 00:51:48.740
more willing to embrace Andy Bernard than Dwight Schrute.

1123
00:51:49.120 --> 00:51:54.080
And so I feel like she could go to her family and be like, well, Dwight bested him in a duel.

1124
00:51:54.080 --> 00:51:57.920
So, you know, clearly Dwight is the dominant man.

1125
00:51:58.280 --> 00:51:59.340
And I have no...

1126
00:51:59.340 --> 00:52:01.860
And that your whole family would accept the results of the duel.

1127
00:52:01.940 --> 00:52:03.180
And I have to go with that.

1128
00:52:03.320 --> 00:52:08.100
So, you know, I mean, I know we all thought Andy was the one, but I don't think Angela

1129
00:52:08.100 --> 00:52:09.600
ever thought Andy was the one.

1130
00:52:09.780 --> 00:52:13.500
And so I think she thinks her family would accept it too.

1131
00:52:13.640 --> 00:52:14.260
Is that crazy?

1132
00:52:14.420 --> 00:52:15.300
But that's what I was thinking.

1133
00:52:15.700 --> 00:52:16.020
Yeah.

1134
00:52:16.140 --> 00:52:18.280
So she's rooting for Dwight to win this duel.

1135
00:52:18.280 --> 00:52:23.040
Because she loves him more and because it would help gain acceptance with her family.

1136
00:52:23.680 --> 00:52:25.980
Well, this duel is happening.

1137
00:52:26.160 --> 00:52:30.280
It is happening in the parking lot at 4 p.m.

1138
00:52:30.680 --> 00:52:32.320
Bring the weapon of your choice.

1139
00:52:32.840 --> 00:52:33.040
Yeah.

1140
00:52:33.920 --> 00:52:35.700
So it's 4 o'clock.

1141
00:52:35.880 --> 00:52:37.360
The duel is beginning.

1142
00:52:38.060 --> 00:52:39.360
Dwight's outside in the parking lot.

1143
00:52:39.520 --> 00:52:41.320
He's yelling, Andy, where are you?

1144
00:52:41.480 --> 00:52:43.060
You know, he's like, are you a coward?

1145
00:52:43.660 --> 00:52:47.280
Everyone else is upstairs watching from the conference room.

1146
00:52:47.280 --> 00:52:50.660
So Angela's saying, I can't believe two men are fighting over me.

1147
00:52:51.340 --> 00:52:53.120
And then Kelly, like, has a dig.

1148
00:52:53.240 --> 00:52:56.380
She's like, well, I guess when you're old, you run out of options or something like that.

1149
00:52:56.400 --> 00:52:57.080
I thought that was really funny.

1150
00:52:57.320 --> 00:52:57.580
Yeah.

1151
00:52:58.680 --> 00:53:00.460
Oscar doesn't think Andy's going to show.

1152
00:53:00.600 --> 00:53:02.140
And they're actually kind of placing bets.

1153
00:53:02.200 --> 00:53:03.500
And Kevin's like, come on.

1154
00:53:03.780 --> 00:53:06.620
But then Dwight sees a note on some bushes.

1155
00:53:06.980 --> 00:53:07.360
Yeah.

1156
00:53:07.460 --> 00:53:08.560
He goes over to read it.

1157
00:53:08.660 --> 00:53:09.340
What is this?

1158
00:53:09.840 --> 00:53:10.240
Yeah.

1159
00:53:10.240 --> 00:53:11.320
What's this note about?

1160
00:53:11.800 --> 00:53:16.700
While he's reading it, Andy does show up very slowly, very quietly.

1161
00:53:17.420 --> 00:53:17.940
Yes.

1162
00:53:18.120 --> 00:53:18.860
In his Prius.

1163
00:53:19.780 --> 00:53:25.220
Well, you know, Jenna, Jen had that one sentence that she had to write this whole episode off of,

1164
00:53:25.320 --> 00:53:25.480
right?

1165
00:53:25.640 --> 00:53:26.440
About the duel.

1166
00:53:26.900 --> 00:53:30.080
This was Paul Lieberstein's idea about the Prius.

1167
00:53:30.240 --> 00:53:34.100
He said, if you go under five miles an hour, it's totally silent.

1168
00:53:35.240 --> 00:53:38.880
And so this is the weapon Andy chooses.

1169
00:53:39.600 --> 00:53:39.880
Yes.

1170
00:53:39.880 --> 00:53:44.580
He is going to pin Dwight up against the bushes.

1171
00:53:44.580 --> 00:53:46.040
He's going to crush him.

1172
00:53:46.220 --> 00:53:49.740
But really, he's only crushing, like, from his kneecaps down.

1173
00:53:50.060 --> 00:53:50.440
Yeah.

1174
00:53:50.560 --> 00:53:51.640
But he's pinned.

1175
00:53:51.900 --> 00:53:53.400
I mean, Dwight can't move.

1176
00:53:53.540 --> 00:53:56.280
Dwight can't hit him with his bike chain anymore.

1177
00:53:56.600 --> 00:53:57.140
Yeah.

1178
00:53:57.320 --> 00:53:59.840
So he starts slamming it on the hood of the car.

1179
00:54:00.020 --> 00:54:01.860
They're screaming at each other.

1180
00:54:01.860 --> 00:54:09.600
At 18 minutes, 16 seconds, Rain shared on the DVD that during this whole screaming match

1181
00:54:09.600 --> 00:54:13.880
between the two of them, they improvise for about 40 minutes.

1182
00:54:14.260 --> 00:54:15.960
Dean said at least 40 minutes.

1183
00:54:16.960 --> 00:54:20.080
Just insults and banter back and forth at each other.

1184
00:54:20.620 --> 00:54:22.380
Dean said there was so much good stuff.

1185
00:54:22.640 --> 00:54:24.520
Oh, I wish we could see that.

1186
00:54:24.720 --> 00:54:26.760
The 40 minutes of them yelling at each other.

1187
00:54:26.760 --> 00:54:27.560
You would watch it.

1188
00:54:27.760 --> 00:54:28.420
Sure.

1189
00:54:28.420 --> 00:54:29.000
I would do, actually.

1190
00:54:29.280 --> 00:54:30.620
They're probably amazing.

1191
00:54:31.320 --> 00:54:38.080
Well, we got a lot of questions about how did we do this scene?

1192
00:54:38.220 --> 00:54:39.660
How did we do this stunt?

1193
00:54:39.880 --> 00:54:41.100
Who was driving?

1194
00:54:41.880 --> 00:54:43.000
Yada, yada.

1195
00:54:43.280 --> 00:54:50.640
Well, I talked to Dean, and he said this was really complicated because we had to shoot

1196
00:54:50.640 --> 00:54:55.960
this scene over two different days from three different locations.

1197
00:54:55.960 --> 00:55:00.860
First, we shot in the parking lot with Rain and Ed.

1198
00:55:01.180 --> 00:55:02.880
They performed the whole thing.

1199
00:55:02.880 --> 00:55:04.060
We shot it.

1200
00:55:04.240 --> 00:55:10.620
And the rest of us were upstairs in Paul's office looking out that window, and the camera

1201
00:55:10.620 --> 00:55:12.040
could whip up to us.

1202
00:55:12.220 --> 00:55:13.320
In real time.

1203
00:55:13.440 --> 00:55:14.300
In real time.

1204
00:55:14.480 --> 00:55:14.900
Yes.

1205
00:55:14.980 --> 00:55:15.920
We watched all of it.

1206
00:55:16.460 --> 00:55:23.980
Then they moved the cameras up to Paul's office to get really tight shots out of the window

1207
00:55:23.980 --> 00:55:30.160
onto the action below, and Rain and Ed had to do it all over again just to get a few little

1208
00:55:30.160 --> 00:55:31.620
shots through the window.

1209
00:55:31.860 --> 00:55:37.140
But then on a different day, we shot inside the actual Dunder Mifflin conference room,

1210
00:55:37.160 --> 00:55:41.880
and this time we had to be careful to not shoot out the window because there was nothing

1211
00:55:41.880 --> 00:55:42.240
there.

1212
00:55:42.240 --> 00:55:43.280
It was just a backdrop.

1213
00:55:43.980 --> 00:55:49.520
And that we were basically looking at nothing, but Dean was shouting out all the action that

1214
00:55:49.520 --> 00:55:50.800
had happened the day before.

1215
00:55:51.620 --> 00:55:51.820
Right.

1216
00:55:52.140 --> 00:55:56.260
He said this was the moment when being an editor on the show really helped him.

1217
00:55:56.400 --> 00:56:01.960
He had kind of cut this whole thing together with a shot list inside his head, and he just

1218
00:56:01.960 --> 00:56:03.580
kept telling people, trust me, trust me.

1219
00:56:03.760 --> 00:56:04.280
Trust me.

1220
00:56:04.360 --> 00:56:04.740
Trust me.

1221
00:56:05.360 --> 00:56:07.000
He could see it, right?

1222
00:56:07.180 --> 00:56:08.020
He could see it.

1223
00:56:08.060 --> 00:56:09.200
He could see the whole thing.

1224
00:56:09.200 --> 00:56:16.020
He said he planned all of these whip pan cuts between the window, between us, all of it.

1225
00:56:16.400 --> 00:56:21.440
And when he got in the editing room, because he edited this episode as well, it actually

1226
00:56:21.440 --> 00:56:25.200
did all come together, and it looked really, really seamless.

1227
00:56:25.580 --> 00:56:28.280
Well, you have to think that Randy Cordray was like, I knew it.

1228
00:56:28.400 --> 00:56:29.100
I knew it.

1229
00:56:29.140 --> 00:56:29.480
Yes!

1230
00:56:29.660 --> 00:56:32.040
That Dean's editing was going to come into play here.

1231
00:56:32.200 --> 00:56:34.800
This is why Dean has to direct this episode.

1232
00:56:34.800 --> 00:56:40.200
But he did say it was a little grueling for the actors, because we had to play these same

1233
00:56:40.200 --> 00:56:45.980
moments over and over and over again, more so than we normally do, and we had to make

1234
00:56:45.980 --> 00:56:48.440
it seem like we were doing it for the first time every time.

1235
00:56:48.920 --> 00:56:56.200
Now, as for the stunt, Randy told us that Ed actually drove the Prius silently through

1236
00:56:56.200 --> 00:56:56.960
the parking lot.

1237
00:56:57.080 --> 00:57:02.200
He said they had stunt doubles standing by for the actual moment of impact.

1238
00:57:02.200 --> 00:57:07.960
They thought that they would have a stunt driver actually drive into a stunt Dwight.

1239
00:57:08.540 --> 00:57:14.420
And then after they were kind of squished, they would place Rain into the bushes.

1240
00:57:14.820 --> 00:57:16.340
And Ed into the car.

1241
00:57:16.480 --> 00:57:16.820
Yes.

1242
00:57:17.020 --> 00:57:22.400
But then on the commentary, didn't Rain say they just kind of ended up doing it themselves?

1243
00:57:23.180 --> 00:57:28.960
Actually, the commentary was Rainn Wilson, Jen Salata, Dean Holland, and Rusty Mahmood,

1244
00:57:28.960 --> 00:57:30.520
who was our first assistant director.

1245
00:57:31.200 --> 00:57:37.700
And they discussed that Ed actually drove into Rain very slowly.

1246
00:57:37.900 --> 00:57:38.600
Oh, my gosh.

1247
00:57:38.600 --> 00:57:40.700
And that it totally worked.

1248
00:57:40.980 --> 00:57:44.280
And those takes of those guys actually doing it were their favorite.

1249
00:57:44.380 --> 00:57:46.160
So those were the ones they used.

1250
00:57:46.280 --> 00:57:48.400
And they did not use takes with the stunt people.

1251
00:57:48.640 --> 00:57:52.520
Well, we also got a fan question from Samantha T, who wanted to know,

1252
00:57:52.520 --> 00:57:55.040
what was up with the fence?

1253
00:57:55.320 --> 00:57:57.960
Like, what was on the other side of it?

1254
00:57:58.080 --> 00:57:59.080
Was it padding?

1255
00:57:59.440 --> 00:58:01.200
Was it an actual fence?

1256
00:58:01.600 --> 00:58:04.000
Was the bumper of the car padded?

1257
00:58:04.340 --> 00:58:06.480
Was Rain really being squashed?

1258
00:58:07.100 --> 00:58:09.280
Well, it was the real bumper of the car.

1259
00:58:09.460 --> 00:58:13.300
And then Rain sent in an audio clip to tell us a little bit about the bushes.

1260
00:58:13.980 --> 00:58:19.200
Oh, I'm so glad you guys are doing the dual fantastic, one of my very favorite episodes.

1261
00:58:19.200 --> 00:58:25.520
And I always loved those episodes where Dwight and Andy got to go head to head.

1262
00:58:25.700 --> 00:58:30.180
I just loved that subplot of that tension.

1263
00:58:30.200 --> 00:58:33.040
And Ed Helms is so funny in this episode.

1264
00:58:33.480 --> 00:58:40.740
But you know what it reminded me of is in college, we studied clowning and Commedia dell'arte.

1265
00:58:40.740 --> 00:58:48.300
